uuid "ac95037f-a14a-513c-ac1a-9a2406593ddc" :question/math-academy-id "q-70106" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y=12 \\\\ 4x+5y=21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $x=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y=12 \\\\ 4x+5y=21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}12 & 2 \\\\ 21 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}12 & 2 \\\\ 21 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7580024-f357-57d4-94f2-85c25e2c144b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parts of Cramer's Rule Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1046d3f3-10cc-5f37-acf8-d2722c6a0ec7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335145} {:answer/id #uuid "99715a8f-f645-565e-ac00-b4f6339a9f0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335146} {:answer/id #uuid "e05b28a5-7f29-5b73-a29b-6413dcf93d26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335147} {:answer/id #uuid "04cddaca-e62d-5675-81a4-77505aaea964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335148} {:answer/id #uuid "f44b49c2-16b2-5a14-ba71-ce062d61989b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04cddaca-e62d-5675-81a4-77505aaea964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335148} :answer-field/id #uuid "59261eff-90ab-5946-8f76-cc562e4bc7c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335144}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6605299f-ff45-5450-b549-1e0c28be5ac3" :question/math-academy-id "q-70200" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=7 \\\\ 3x-4y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as \n$x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|}$, where ${D}_{x}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=7 \\\\ 3x-4y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7580024-f357-57d4-94f2-85c25e2c144b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parts of Cramer's Rule Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75d42042-434d-5a69-aacc-193880c3c2d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335152} {:answer/id #uuid "5506e7ea-4684-502f-a34b-5360e1da77aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335153} {:answer/id #uuid "1c4cff56-39c3-58b0-90a7-952e85dfe6cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335154} {:answer/id #uuid "1d7440b8-7c4a-5380-8837-6cd2205c7b52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335155} {:answer/id #uuid "126916aa-c8be-5d9d-822a-919524a2ad50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c4cff56-39c3-58b0-90a7-952e85dfe6cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335154} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b8c6a4e-1f22-5f7e-b077-0f7db42cd782" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d47b44f-bbb3-54e7-8ca3-2db255852117" :question/math-academy-id "q-70201" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,3x-3y=1 \\\\ -x+2y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $y$ can be written as $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}$, where ${D}_{y}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,3x-3y=1 \\\\ -x+2y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & \\,\\,1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbd05303-f84e-5c67-b25f-01fc8466c943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335159} {:answer/id #uuid "744e467e-bda6-53b3-b523-5d32ebad0211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335160} {:answer/id #uuid "4fbbbcb1-bc09-5aad-a102-41f1f825662b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335161} {:answer/id #uuid "3791b02d-ebb5-586f-a80d-c9c0f6c0d972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335162} {:answer/id #uuid "4330df1e-c834-580d-9cec-35670e81873f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fbbbcb1-bc09-5aad-a102-41f1f825662b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335161} :answer-field/id #uuid "37292bee-6ead-58b3-9354-c6080811ad1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "745a2d2f-9203-593c-9a03-87c0afb1d76b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70252" :question/problem "Let $⟨-1,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+ky=-4 \\\\ 3x-4y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=-2|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}| & =-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335164 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40547905-338c-5eb2-998a-423d4496c5d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335166} {:answer/id #uuid "6b182097-03f6-5ca4-a97c-285a71bba37f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335167} {:answer/id #uuid "b386dfd2-c25f-5723-81a9-60769cc66da9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335168} {:answer/id #uuid "4c39b7b3-7ac3-5b42-a1f9-647ae49a032c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335169} {:answer/id #uuid "9ee164b0-ad4b-5be9-a49c-b36ee706afd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b386dfd2-c25f-5723-81a9-60769cc66da9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335168} :answer-field/id #uuid "093501fe-892b-586c-b246-d7c365451259" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0eb9ac70-c138-5a1e-a3c5-58f7492a13a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-77401" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,1⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=k \\\\ x+4y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- $|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=5$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=-7$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=13$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =12+1 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{13} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}]}
